                <pb facs="0398" n="384" sameAs="frus:frus1950v06/pg384"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>Between July 20 and 24, high-level and wide-ranging Anglo-American discussions
                    were held in Washington by delegations led by Ambassador <pb facs="0399" n="385"
                        xml:id="pg385"/> at Large Philip Jessup and Chairman of the Joint Chiefs of
                    Staff Omar Bradley for the United States and British Ambassador Sir Oliver
                    Franks and Lord Tedder, Chairman of the British Joint Services Mission in
                    Washington, for the United Kingdom. The talks, dealing with problems arising
                    from or magnified by the Korean conflict, were exploratory in nature. The text
                    of the Agreed Joint Memorandum resulting from the talks is scheduled for
                    publication in volume III. For extracts of those portions dealing with the Far
                    East, see <ref target="frus:frus1950v07/pg_462">volume VII, page 462</ref>.
                    Material on the conversations and records of the individual meetings are
                    contained in Department of State file 611.41/8–450.</p>
            </div>
